### Practical 7 — Cell Viability Assessment

### Objective
- To distinguish viable and non-viable cells.
- To determine the percentage of viable cells in a sample.

### What to Learn
- Viable vs non-viable cells
- Cell viability
- Viability percentage
- Cell-counting-based viability assessment

### Practical Work
- Mix the cell sample with an appropriate viability indicator.
- Count viable and non-viable cells separately.
- Calculate total cell number.
- Calculate percentage viability.
- Record and interpret the result.

### Expected Outcome
- Cell viability assessment
- Quantitative calculation
- Data interpretation


